From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI: plain colours instead of wallpaper gradients

The scrims of the notification shade, the background of the recents screen
and that of the power menu are gradients between two colours taken from the
wallpaper. A display with few grey levels shows a gradient as bands (PW3 Test
V34, e-paper with 16 levels: concentric rings behind the quick settings).

All of them get their colours from SysuiColorExtractor. With
config_gradientColors=false it hands out one plain colour instead: white
where the extracted colours are for dark text, black where they are for
light text. How opaque each user draws them is unchanged.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/colorextraction/SysuiColorExtractor.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/colorextraction/SysuiColorExtractor.java
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 import android.app.WallpaperColors;
 import android.app.WallpaperManager;
